      "title": "Bastion SSH open to the whole internet",
      "description": "The bastion security group accepts SSH on port 22 from 0.0.0.0/0. Any host on the internet can reach the jump host. Attackers can brute force or exploit SSH on the bastion, which leads straight to the app hosts. Limit the ingress to the on-call engineers' office or VPN CIDR ranges through a variable. Alternatively use SSM Session Manager and drop the ingress.",
      "suggested_change": "    cidr_blocks = var.bastion_allowed_cidrs",
      "source": "trivy:AWS-0107",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The bastion security group accepts SSH on port 22 from 0.0.0.0/0. Any host on the internet can reach the jump host.",
      "consequence": "Attackers can brute force or exploit SSH on the bastion, which leads straight to the app hosts.",
      "fix": "Limit the ingress to the on-call engineers' office or VPN CIDR ranges through a variable. Alternatively use SSM Session Manager and drop the ingress."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
