      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "file_path": "infra/bastion.tf",
      "line_number": 24,
      "line_end": 32,
      "title": "Standalone rule on a security group with inline rules",
      "description": "The app_from_bastion rule attaches to aws_security_group.app, which already defines inline ingress and egress blocks in main.tf. Terraform does not support mixing the two styles on one group. Each apply of the app group removes the SSH rule and the next apply adds it again. Engineers lose bastion access unpredictably and plans never settle. Move the SSH rule into an inline ingress block on aws_security_group.app. Alternatively convert all app group rules to standalone rule resources.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
