      "title": "Orders database marked publicly accessible",
      "description": "The orders RDS instance sets publicly_accessible to true. AWS then gives the database endpoint a public IP address. The orders data becomes reachable from the internet once the VPC has an internet gateway. The VPC has none, so AWS also rejects the create. Set publicly_accessible to false so the database stays on the private subnets.",
      "suggested_change": "  publicly_accessible     = false",
      "source": "trivy:AWS-0180",
      "candidate": "c2",
      "notes": [],
